                <pb facs="0431" n="337" sameAs="frus:frus1930v03/pg337"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.5048/200: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Carter</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-01-18T16:00:00-05:00">January 18, 1930—4
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>5. Your 6, January 14, 5 p.m. Johnson will be accompanied by a competent
                    secretary. They sail from Rotterdam February 21. He will keep Embassy at London
                    informed of his movements while in Europe.</p>
                <p>Wharton is instructed to consult with Johnson at most convenient point in Europe
                    while en route. His travel expenses authorized subject to travel
                    regulations.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cotton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
